          "exampleId": "EX_GU_JEEMAIN2027_CHE_8ADB0D17_01_CLASSIFY_SUBSTANCES",
          "title": "Classifying Homogeneous and Heterogeneous Systems",
          "problemStatement": "Classify each of the following as a homogeneous mixture, heterogeneous mixture, element, or compound: (i) Air, (ii) Pure Water, (iii) Sodium, (iv) Sand in water.",
          "stepByStepSolution": [
            "Step 1: (i) Air is a homogeneous mixture of gases with uniform composition throughout.",
            "Step 2: (ii) Pure Water ($H_2O$) is a chemical compound with fixed 2:1 hydrogen-to-oxygen atomic ratio.",
            "Step 3: (iii) Sodium ($Na$) is a chemical element consisting of a single type of atom.",
            "Step 4: (iv) Sand in water forms a heterogeneous mixture with distinct macroscopic phases."
          ],
          "finalAnswer": "Air = Homogeneous mixture; Water = Compound; Sodium = Element; Sand in water = Heterogeneous mixture.",
